  "details": "There’s some driving worlds, it seems to affect the ones that just use the joystick for driving and not anything else like more recent ones do with hand steering and holding the trigger to accelerate etc. But it seems to only affect steamvr with this new update. A good example would be the “100+ cars” driving world. If you try getting in any of the cars and attempt to drive, it won’t move. And this seems to only affect steamvr inputs. On quest the cars still work, and getting into the car and then using the keyboard to move still works even while in vr. And it course it works in desktop too. It just refuses to detect the joystick input on vr controllers ONLY for steamvr. I’ve also tested a xbox controller in the cars while in vr and it works for that too. I don’t what this new update did to the controls but it’s frustrating.",
